cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use T1DUJxUoM in academic work, please cite the archived software release and the source-code repository using the metadata below."

title: "T1DUJxUoM: Causal Plausibility versus Forecast Accuracy in Patient-Specific Type 1 Diabetes Digital Twins"
type: software

abstract: "T1DUJxUoM is the reproducibility companion for a retrained (60/20/20 chronological train/validation/test split) 7-arm ablation of physics-guided LSTM digital twins for Type 1 Diabetes. It includes the training pipeline (direct glucose prediction, stochastic glucose masking, double-monotonicity loss), evaluation scripts (multi-horizon rollout RMSE, naive-persistence baseline, insulin/carbohydrate dose-response, and an in-silico counterfactual safety panel), and configuration files needed to reproduce all tables and figures in the accompanying paper. It supersedes and replaces the results reported in the earlier T1DUJxUoM v3.0.0 release (10.5281/zenodo.18434352), which used a different evaluation split and is now superseded."

